CVE-2024-29025 exploits **ASN.1 encoding flaws** in OpenSSL’s X.509 parser. Attackers craft a certificate with:
```
SEQUENCE {
  SEQUENCE {
    OBJECT IDENTIFIER commonName (2.5.4.3)
    UTF8String "*.example.com"
  }
  SEQUENCE {
    ...
    SEQUENCE {
      OBJECT IDENTIFIER id-ce-nameConstraints (2.5.29.30)
      OCTET STRING (malformed padding)
    }
  }
}
```
This bypasses **nameConstraints** validation (RFC 5280). Tools: **OpenSSL 3.0.8**, **Certigo**. Real-world: **2024 MITM attack on Cloudflare** via malicious certificates.

**Mitigation**: Patch to **OpenSSL 3.0.14**, enforce **strict name checks**.

